{
  "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
  "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "S.D. Warren Company",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Presumpscot River is a single body of water, as that term was used in last year's Miccosukee decision. Warren's position is that the flowing of that single body of water through Warren's five dams is not a discharge into that same single body of water."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Chief Justice Roberts: Mr. Kayatta, if I took a drum of water out of the river and put it in the garage next to the river for 5 years, and, 5 years later, came out and poured that drum of water back into the river, is that a discharge into the river?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Counsel. General Rowe?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Didn't -- didn't that case involved the -- a violation there -- involve the addition of a pollutant? And there was no addition of a pollutant, because the water was equally polluted on each side."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rowe",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "section 401 came from section 21(b) of the Water Quality Improvement Act of 1970."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the question -- maybe it just -- I don't understand, totally, how the Clean Water Act works, but I thought that what we're talking in this statute is a State rule that's called the State Clean Water Act rule. It's a creature of the Clean Water Act, isn't it? A water quality standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rowe",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0002-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The word \"discharge,\" again, in 1970, under the 21(b), was given a broad definition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0002-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States submits that the operation of Petitioner's hydropower facilities results in a discharge into the navigable waters within the meaning of section 401 of the Clean Water Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0002-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I respectfully disagree, Your Honor, because, in Miccosukee, it addressed the specific question of whether or not there is an addition. And, in the much-quoted soup-ladle example, what it was talking about, in that instance, was taking a ladle of soup, removing it from the pot, and adding it back. The pouring back of the soup into the pot is a discharge, it's a flowing or issuing out. It's not an addition, because nothing is being added to the soup."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Minear",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The dictionary definition of \"discharge\" nowhere speaks of \"addition.\" Petitioners have not pointed to any dictionary definition that speaks in terms of an addition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Do you know what FERC's --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Do you know what FERC's position is --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Do you agree that a State could adopt water quality standards that would, in effect, preclude hydroelectric power in the State?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "consensus position of the United States. This brief has been coordinated not only with EPA and FERC, but also the Department of the Interior and the Army Corps of Engineers. This is the position of the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Minear",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "One often talks about, for instance, the fresh water above the dam being discharged into the fresh waters below. That's -- there's nothing unusual about this, because we're talking about the characteristic of a water that might be shared by the water that's upstream and contained in the dam and is also a characteristic of the water below."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-04-1527",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5d2a5596e168ca777e1b2f21e0bfdc10bfef66908a419d1a3054c42ed1e3206b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5d2a5596e168-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "[Whereupon, at 12:34 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.]"
    }
